    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** anchoring the lineup, boasting an elite efficiency score of 81.88. His matchup against Tanner Gordon is the day's premier opportunity; between a favorable park, a strong platoon advantage, and Gordon\u2019s slow delivery\u2014which plays perfectly into our organizational focus on stolen base efficiency\u2014**Gunnar Henderson** is positioned for a high-ceiling performance. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (73.39) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) are strong plays, as both benefit from dynamic platoon advantages against right-handed pitching, providing excellent stability across the run-production categories.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves the balancing of speed-based upside against matchup projections. **Drake Baldwin** (70.50) secured the C2 spot by virtue of his leadoff status and high xwOBA against right-handed pitching, narrowly edging out the lower-scoring depth options. Meanwhile, the bench remains thin due to the inactivity of **Kyle Tucker** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and we continue to monitor the long-term status of **Andy Pages** and **Jordan Westburg** on the IL. While players like **Nasim Nunez** and **Coby Mayo** landed on the lower end of the startable spectrum, their inclusion is primarily driven by their high stolen base potential against vulnerable pitchers. We are proceeding under the assumption that all lineup positions hold, but with \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board, any late-scratch adjustments in order could shift the daily efficiency scores for **Liam Hicks** or **Dominic Smith** significantly; keep a close eye on final batting order confirmations to ensure no unexpected drop-offs in slot value occur.",
